  "query": "A quiet, elegiac film that lingers in the texture of memory — long takes, soft natural light, characters who circle absence rather than confront it. Loss is treated as a slow tide rather than a single rupture; the camera trusts silence and small gestures to carry feeling.",
  "excluded_films": []
}
```

